Q: css task without class and id A: <p>As Alex said, &quot;element selector will apply style to all hyperlinks&quot;<br />
Let's guess HTML, then I can show you the CSS(without using ID, class, and inline CSS)</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;Please click&lt;a data-link=&quot;user-one&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;Please click&lt;a data-link=&quot;user-two&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>To style each anchor tag separately, I considered different attributes for each.<br />
Here is the CSS to reach your goal by using the attribute selector:</p>
<pre><code>[data-link=&quot;user-one&quot;] {
    background-color: blue;
    color: yellow;
}

[data-link=&quot;user-two&quot;] {
    background-color: brown;
    color: green;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Or you can use combinators based on your HTML structure.<br />
Please share your HTML, then I can show you all eventualities.</p>
